Q: jQuery removeClass and addClass within a function
A: <p>As thatidiotguy said, you're removing the class in the wrong place.  You want something like this:</p>

<pre><code>jQuery(".navitem").click(function (event) {
    event.preventDefault();

    jQuery(".navitem").removeClass("active");
    jQuery(this).addClass("active");
});
</code></pre>

<p>Edit: And also, no need for the <code>javascript:loadTab();</code> in your <code>a</code> tags.  Change their <code>href</code> attributes to <code>#</code>:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;ul id="nav" class="nav"&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;a class="navitem active" href="#"&gt;My Profile &lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;a class="navitem search" href="#"&gt; Search &lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;a class="navitem" href="#"&gt;Favorites &lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Also, I added <code>event.preventDefault();</code> in the <code>click</code> event handler for the links.</p>

